{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ray-exists-metric","title":"lem:ray-exists-metric","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":70,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:ray-exists-metric","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:ray-exists-metric","line":131,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Rays from noncompact spaces: metric version]\n\\label{lem:ray-exists-metric}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-window, def:has-min-segments}\n\n\n\n\n\nIf $M$ is a noncompact proper metric space with minimizing segments,\nthen every $p\\in M$ is the initial point of a minimizing ray.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing}\nProperness and noncompactness imply that $M$ is unbounded. Choose\n$q_k$ with $d(p,q_k)\\ge k$ and minimizing segments from $p$ to $q_k$.\nAfter anchoring them at $p$, Lemma~\\ref{lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing}\non $[0,\\infty)$ produces the required ray.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Rays from noncompact spaces: metric version] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7261792d6578697374732d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">morgan-tian</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-window\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-window</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Ahas-min-segments\">↗ def:has-min-segments</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is a noncompact proper metric space with minimizing segments, then every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> is the initial point of a minimizing ray.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aultrafilter-limit-minimizing\">↗ lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing</a> Properness and noncompactness imply that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is unbounded. Choose <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_k$\">$q_k$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(p,q_k)\\ge k$\">$d(p,q_k)\\ge k$</span> and minimizing segments from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_k$\">$q_k$</span>. After anchoring them at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>, Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aultrafilter-limit-minimizing\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a756c74726166696c7465722d6c696d69742d6d696e696d697a696e67\">1</a> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[0,\\infty )$\">$[0,\\infty )$</span> produces the required ray. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ends-differ-at-compact","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","title":"def:has-min-segments","label":"def:has-min-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","title":"lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","label":"lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#ends","title":"ends","label":"ends"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ray-exists-metric","title":"lem:ray-exists-metric","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Rays from noncompact spaces: metric version]\n\\label{lem:ray-exists-metric}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-window, def:has-min-segments}\n\n\n\n\n\nIf $M$ is a noncompact proper metric space with minimizing segments,\nthen every $p\\in M$ is the initial point of a minimizing ray.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing}\nProperness and noncompactness imply that $M$ is unbounded. Choose\n$q_k$ with $d(p,q_k)\\ge k$ and minimizing segments from $p$ to $q_k$.\nAfter anchoring them at $p$, Lemma~\\ref{lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing}\non $[0,\\infty)$ produces the required ray.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","title":"def:has-min-segments","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","title":"lem:ultrafilter-limit-minimizing","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}